#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 240 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 the object routes float messages to the first outlet
and all other messages (bang \, symbol \, list \, any) to the second
outlet;
#X text 240 138 by default a list containing a single float is treated
as a float. Set @strict to true to disable this behavior and route
such lists to the second outlet;
#X text 240 193 to get properties \, use the [prop.get] object \, since
all messages (including property requests) are passed through;
#X text 240 248 the object can be used to separate numeric values from
other messages \, for example to route numbers to a display and everything
else to a logger;
